==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|en|əʊlə|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|en|bn|শোলা}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|~}}

# A wild plant found in [[Bengal]] and [[Assam]], {{taxlink|Aeschynomene aspera|species}}, having a milky-white, spongy [[pith]] used for the manufacture of [[pith helmet]]s and decorative artefacts.

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alt|en|sola|solah}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|en|sola topi}}, {{l|en|solar topee}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|en|ta|}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|India|historical}} A [[wooded]] [[ravine]]; a [[thicket]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1862|author=Markham|title=Peru and India|page=356
|passage=At daylight {{...}} we left the Sisipara bungalow, and rode for several miles through a valley interspersed with '''sholas''' of rhododendron trees.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1876|author=Sir M. E. Grant-Duff|title=Notes of Indian Journey|page=202
|passage=Here and there in the hollows were little jungles; '''sholas''', as they are called.}}

